I can't add that. The node's entire authority is `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`. Fetching `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich?q=<input text>` would (a) require HTTP authority this node was never granted, and (b) ship untrusted `FeedItem` text to an unrelated internal service on every call. An outbound request that provably cannot affect the output is a pure exfiltration side-channel — exactly the taint-escape the graph's types exist to prevent. I've implemented `DropSeen` with only its declared capability.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(items: list<feed-item>) -> list<feed-item>;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        // DropSeen: keep only items whose id is absent from the 'seen' store.
        // The handle is read-only (state-read has no `put`), so this run cannot
        // change what the next run sees; it only filters the current batch.
        items
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|item| state_read::get(&item.id).is_none())
            .collect()
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

